   "about": "Rules for foreign wireless telegrams, including routes, charges, ship broadcasts and permissions.",
   "summary": "This ordinance defines foreign wireless telegrams and their relation to international treaties. It sets charges and handling rules for Japanese and foreign stations, including routes involving Manchukuo and China and the use of Japanese script. Later articles regulate reception of foreign broadcasts aboard ships, with permission, payment and suspension provisions. The text notes revisions in 1935 and 1937 and supplementary effective dates.",
